{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/760183-so-i-m-thinking","id":760183,"title":"So I'm thinking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-07T13:39:17-08:00","id":760183,"title":"So I'm thinking","content":"This month is my B-Day and Christmas is the month after (aren't I fuggin lucky?). I've been considering buying the hard covers of Scion, since I don't trust buying the digital PDF's in case my computer crashes or some shit.<br /> <br /> I think I've got the whole Scion series on my wishlist over on DriveThru. (Hero, Demigod, God, and Companion.) except for Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> So for somebody who's new to the game, what do I need to know about in regards to playing the game properly? Is there a core rule book, or does Hero cover that? Also, does it only use 10 sided die like World of Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T14:50:34-08:00","id":760236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/760183-so-i-m-thinking#post760183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This month is my B-Day and Christmas is the month after (aren't I fuggin lucky?). I've been considering buying the hard covers of Scion, since I don't trust buying the digital PDF's in case my computer crashes or some shit.<br /> <br /> I think I've got the whole Scion series on my wishlist over on DriveThru. (Hero, Demigod, God, and Companion.) except for Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> So for somebody who's new to the game, what do I need to know about in regards to playing the game properly? Is there a core rule book, or does Hero cover that? Also, does it only use 10 sided die like World of Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>D10 only, yes.<br /> You need Hero to start, and yes, Hero covers the core rules. The stuff you need to know at Demigod level is Demigod, and stuff you need to know when you reach God-hood is in God. Ragnarok is an in-depth campaign book for the Norse gods, and contains the Frost and Illusion all-purpose Purviews. Companion has some expanded rules and boons for all levels, as well as 3 new (fully formed) Pantheons, their Godrealms, Underworlds \u200band their Titan enemies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:49:34-08:00","id":760290,"title":"","content":"Aww, so Illusion and Frost aren't in the core purview? How can I play a Trickster if I can't mess with peoples sense of reality? Anyways, thanks for the information. ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, there's something else I noticed some players bring up on here. How much information on each of the pantheons do the books provide? Some people on the forums commented they didn't know anything about certain pantheons, which leads me to believe the book isn't very descriptive. Personally, the only pantheon I'm really familiar with is the Dodekatheon. All others on the list I've only got second hand knowledge about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-07-2015, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T17:30:43-08:00","id":760363,"title":"","content":"You don't need Illusion to be a trickster... Epic levels of Manipulation, Charisma and even Appearance have Knacks to trick and manipulate others with relative ease. Ragnarok also has a few useful Knacks that are worth a look see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T20:46:05-08:00","id":760463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/760183-so-i-m-thinking?p=760290#post760290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, so Illusion and Frost aren't in the core purview? How can I play a Trickster if I can't mess with peoples sense of reality? Anyways, thanks for the information. ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, there's something else I noticed some players bring up on here. How much information on each of the pantheons do the books provide? Some people on the forums commented they didn't know anything about certain pantheons, which leads me to believe the book isn't very descriptive. Personally, the only pantheon I'm really familiar with is the Dodekatheon. All others on the list I've only got second hand knowledge about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadowstripe is correct: you can still do a LOT of Trickster stuff with Epic Socials. The Illusion Purview is definitely a bonus, but it's not absolutely essential. The good news is that the Ragnarok book is possibly the best book out of the Scion series, so if you can get it, you won't be disappointed.<br /> <br /> The books do a good job of laying out the basics of the Pantheons. Each god gets a basic write-up that gives you some idea about what you're dealing with. Certain Pantheons, however, are better written than others. The Dodekatheon and the Aesir are pretty accurate, but more than one expert has complained about the poor writing of the Loa and the Atzlanti.<br /> <br /> The books are descriptive enough that you can get by, but if you feel inclined to research the mythologies of the pantheons, you can do this for free thanks to the Internet. Almost all the pantheons and their stories can be found online, so it's not that hard to familiarize yourself with them.<br /> <br /> As others have said: Hero, Demigod, and God are essential if you want to explore all the tiers of power in Scion. As always, however, the caveat must be repeated: Scion's system works fine at Hero level, but at Demigod and upward, things begin to break down. By God-level, the system is pretty much a destroyed mess. I haven't met a Scion group yet that plays the game without substantial house ruling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T21:38:38-08:00","id":760484,"title":"","content":"I have heard that by the time you get past hero level, the mortal world is pretty much powerless to resist you. But this is a game about playing gods in training. I would expect nothing less in order for the story to hold up. Especially when taking our mythology into account where deities were able to hold planetary bodies over their head with brute strength alone. It also sounds like the Greater Titans are living concepts more than physical beings, which I think explains why something as powerful as the gods have such difficulty fighting them. It's much harder to slay the idea of chaos than those who serve it, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> World of Darkness is what got me introduced to WhiteWolf in the first place. While I do enjoy the supernatural horror setting of that game, I think the idea of a super hero theme environment is also appealing. And let's not pretend they aren't super heroes, the whole Fate Binding thing practically screams &quot;Secret Identity&quot; for players looking to avoid such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-08-2015, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T06:06:04-08:00","id":760628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/760183-so-i-m-thinking?p=760484#post760484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have heard that by the time you get past hero level, the mortal world is pretty much powerless to resist you. But this is a game about playing gods in training. I would expect nothing less in order for the story to hold up. Especially when taking our mythology into account where deities were able to hold planetary bodies over their head with brute strength alone. It also sounds like the Greater Titans are living concepts more than physical beings, which I think explains why something as powerful as the gods have such difficulty fighting them. It's much harder to slay the idea of chaos than those who serve it, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> World of Darkness is what got me introduced to WhiteWolf in the first place. While I do enjoy the supernatural horror setting of that game, I think the idea of a super hero theme environment is also appealing. And let's not pretend they aren't super heroes, the whole Fate Binding thing practically screams &quot;Secret Identity&quot; for players looking to avoid such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just that mortals stop being a credible threat to you at the higher levels. The system itself falls apart, even when you're fighting giants and dragons and other gods. I'm not as system-savvy as others on this board, so I'm not the best qualified to talk about the system's inadequacies, but it's been almost universally acknowledged as a real problem and one of the main motivators for the 2E reboot.<br /> <br /> Among the biggest problems are the fact that Dex pretty much reigns supreme among the combat stats. If your character doesn't have Epic Dex, he/she won't hit anything in combat that does have have it. You also can't evade incoming attacks from Dex-heavy characters. So if you have a character design that doesn't feature extreme Dexterity, then that character is going to be in big trouble in combat. That's just one example.<br /> <br /> And Scions are totally superheroes. If Scions want to avoid Fatebinding, then they do need to try to maintain a low profile. On the other hand, Fatebinding can offer benefits as well as drawbacks, so a Scion who chooses to throw caution to the wind isn't exactly doomed either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T10:22:19-08:00","id":760737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/760183-so-i-m-thinking#post760183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've been considering buying the hard covers of Scion, since I don't trust buying the digital PDF's in case my computer crashes or some shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just a one-and-done purchase. If you buy something on DriveThruRPG it's yours forever. It's added to your DTRPG library, and you can re-download it again at any point. In fact, it also has the ability to download directly to a Dropbox account, so you don't even have to store anything on your hard drive after you've bought it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:37:23-08:00","id":760795,"title":"","content":"So I found a site that gives a general explanation of the Purviews... Apparently the level 10 Yankee boon is a fucking nuke. Yeah, I think that sounds about right, just nuke the titans!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://scion-mmp.wikidot.com/industry-boons\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://d3g0gp89917ko0.cloudfront.net/v--291054f06006/common--images/social/twitter.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://scion-mmp.wikidot.com/industry-boons\" target=\"_blank\"> Industry Boons - Scion: Monsters and Mosh Pits </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://scion-mmp.wikidot.com/industry-boons\" target=\"_blank\"> http://scion-mmp.wikidot.com/industry-boons </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T09:53:09-08:00","id":763195,"title":"","content":"Okay, I need to know if I messed up. I went and ordered Hero and Demigod, but I accidentally typed in my personal address instead of my PO Box. Turns out, we don't get mail delivered directly to my door.<br /> <br /> Does anybody know of a way to get in contact with Drive Thru and inform them of this mistake before they send out the books?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDITED:</b><br /> <br /> Nevermind, got through to them. Changed the deliver from postal service to UPS. DriveThru doesn't do PO boxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-11-2015, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T19:22:58-08:00","id":765293,"title":"","content":"The issue with high-level Scion play is that Epic Attributes work on an exponential curve. Once you get to the God or high-Demigod level, one dot of difference in, say, Epic Dexterity, is a difference that is almost completely insurmountable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T20:51:42-08:00","id":765327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/760183-so-i-m-thinking?p=765293#post765293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with high-level Scion play is that Epic Attributes work on an exponential curve. Once you get to the God or high-Demigod level, one dot of difference in, say, Epic Dexterity, is a difference that is almost completely insurmountable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about the Star Purview? Doesn't that give you time-space powers? Like say, slowing somebody down or just stopping them in place.<br /> <br /> Anyways, what are some house rules people like to use to help balance out the dexterity?<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, one final note, how high do Epic Attributes go to? I found a website dedicated to the game, but it only lists up to Epic Attribute level 3, which doesn't sound like characters would be bench pressing mountains if the most they get is a lousy 2,000 lbs added to their strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-13-2015, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T21:26:01-08:00","id":765339,"title":"","content":"Epic Attributes go up to 11, IIRC. Carrying on with doubling the number of successes each time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T21:30:58-08:00","id":765340,"title":"","content":"So at Epic Strength 11, you could lift an additional 512,000 lbs. Which is about 256 tons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T21:40:31-08:00","id":765344,"title":"","content":"Well, more to the point (and I just realised I don't have my Scion stuff on this computer), the difference between Epic Dexterity 10 and 11 is... something like 20 successes? More? I can't actually recall the number here, but it's completely ridiculous, and to the point, makes a task that's <i>trivial</i> to a character with Epic Dexterity 11 almost impossible for a character with Epic Dexterity 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T21:51:49-08:00","id":765347,"title":"","content":"In actual fact, I forgot about Ultimate Attributes. :V<br /> <br /> Basically, most mechanical effects of an Epic Attribute go up to the 10-dot level (like Attributes themselves do). You get 46 bonus successes at Epic Attribute 10, as opposed to 37 at 9- which is still pretty much insurmountable unless you're <i>very</i> lucky. <br /> <br /> (On a side note, Epic Strength 10 actually gives you 1,250,000,000 lbs of lifting strength, which can be increased with Knacks.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T22:42:05-08:00","id":765360,"title":"","content":"Wait, one and a quarter billion pounds of strength? Did I do the math wrong? I just multiplied 500 by 2 on a calculator 11 times.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's 625,000 tons!<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, holy shit, 20+ successes on dexterity is bullshit. I mean I get it from a story telling point, you're playing a character who is quite literally fast as lightning and elusive as the wind, but from a game mechanic stand point, that would need to be dialed back. I could see the idea of home brewing a level cap on the automatic success thing (no higher than 5 at the most), while still unlocking special abilities or knacks as you increase its effectiveness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Edit:</b></span> Okay, I think I figured it out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hero - Epic Attributes multiply the effect by 2<br /> <br /> Demigod - Epic Attributes multiply the effect by 5<br /> <br /> God - Epic Attributes multiply the effect by 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-14-2015, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T16:33:59-08:00","id":766632,"title":"","content":"Soooo yeah, that whole automatic success thing sounds good from a story telling point, but not in terms of gameplay mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I had to home brew the rules, I would remove the auto success and replace it with each level of Epic Attribute increases the respective dice pool by 1. For example, 7 Epic Strength would add 7 die to your Strength rolls, and so on.<br /> <br /> Does that sound like something more appropriate, or would that dramatically reduce the effectiveness of such abilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T17:29:24-08:00","id":766673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/760183-so-i-m-thinking?p=763195#post763195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I need to know if I messed up. I went and ordered Hero and Demigod, but I accidentally typed in my personal address instead of my PO Box. Turns out, we don't get mail delivered directly to my door.<br /> <br /> Does anybody know of a way to get in contact with Drive Thru and inform them of this mistake before they send out the books?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDITED:</b><br /> <br /> Nevermind, got through to them. Changed the deliver from postal service to UPS. DriveThru doesn't do PO boxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's odd... I've gotten DriveThru books delivered to my PO Box no problem, but then I guess that's side tracking this thread a bit.<br /> <br /> I now return you to your regularly scheduled discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T06:03:33-08:00","id":767013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/760183-so-i-m-thinking?p=766673#post766673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's odd... I've gotten DriveThru books delivered to my PO Box no problem, but then I guess that's side tracking this thread a bit.<br /> <br /> I now return you to your regularly scheduled discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Our mailman doesn't deliver directly to the house and I sent a request to DriveThru asking to change the address to PO Box. They replied with an email saying their current delivery process doesn't support PO. Boxes, but they were nice enough to cancel the delivery and change the money I used into account credit. I reused the credit to change the deliver to UPS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T11:49:16-08:00","id":768635,"title":"","content":"<b>Good News:</b> The books were delivered successfully!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bad News:</b> I've only got a pair of 10 sided dice... this is going to be a hell of a lot of re-rolls!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}